  :itonami.blueprint/implemented-slice
  "Stock Advisor ⊣ Warehouse Stock Governor, a REAL compiled
  `kotoba-lang/langgraph` StateGraph (`:intake -> :advise -> :govern
  -> :decide -+-> :commit / :request-approval -> :commit / :hold`),
  append-only audit ledger. Replaces a prior state with NO StateGraph
  wiring whatsoever: there was no `actor.cljc` at all, `deps.edn` had
  an empty top-level `:deps {}` (langgraph wasn't even declared), and
  no `advisor.cljc` (no mock/LLM injection boundary existed). The
  repo's `warehouse-stock.governor` (discrepancy-threshold +
  sku/bin-provenance checks) and `warehouse-stock.store`
  (`record-event!`) were real but only ever exercised by tests, never
  by a running actor. Now: a genuine `interrupt-before
  #{:request-approval}` + in-memory checkpointer pauses
  `:human-approval` verdicts for real human sign-off (`approve!`
  resumes the SAME compiled graph via the graph's own
  `:request-approval -> :commit` edge, not a hand-rolled parallel
  commit path), and BOTH `:commit` and `:hold` durably append to the
  real audit ledger (`store/record-event!`) — a held HARD-violation
  proposal is now also queryable audit history via the store's new
  `events` accessor, not silently discarded. Store gained a
  `DatomicStore` (via `kotoba-lang/langchain-store`, no hand-rolled
  EDN-blob codec) alongside `MemStore`, proven ≡ by a new
  store-contract test. Three ops (`:receive` / `:pick` / `:count`),
  all `:effect :propose` only. HARD invariants (unregistered sku/bin,
  non-`:propose` effect, a `:count` event whose discrepancy from the
  sku's `expected-qty` exceeds `discrepancy-threshold` at below
  `:high` safety-class) always `:hold` — a large discrepancy can never
  be auto-corrected, only recorded and escalated; low-confidence
  proposals also require human sign-off. 14 tests / 63 assertions
  green, clj-kondo 0 errors."
  :itonami.blueprint/id "cloud-itonami-isco-4321"
